The baseline CMC model should be compared against the receptor-informed model in a way that keeps the optimisation procedure fair. My current understanding is that the baseline model should also be fitted with comparable EM-start handling rather than being compared against a receptor-informed model that had many more opportunities to optimise.

This point still needs to be checked carefully in the code, especially how the baseline model is initialised relative to the winning receptor-informed model and/or sigma setting.

## Interpretation after the meeting
